{"availability":"available","full":"Dream-World-Coder/depuzzled","name":"depuzzled","description":"A 311 byte Klotski solver in C++","category":"Other","language":"C++","stars":6,"forks":1,"created":"2026-09-30T04:17:41Z","updated":"2026-10-01T04:34:38Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["bfs","cpp","game","graph","klotski","klotski-engine","statespace"],"demo":null,"color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","stars":6,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A 311 byte Klotski solver in C++ Give it a board, it finds the shortest way to slide the pieces until the big square reaches the goal.","Klotski is a sliding block puzzle. You have a box that is 4 cells wide and 5 cells tall. Inside the box there are blocks of different shapes, and only two empty cells. You can slide a block into an empty cell next to it. You cannot lift blocks or turn them.","The goal is to move the big square to the bottom middle of the box. In this program the goal is exactly this: the top left cell of the big square must sit at row 3, column 1 (counting from 0). That means the big square fills rows 3 and 4, columns 1 and 2."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Dream-World-Coder/depuzzled/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"71805029c6a10093e900c6f3a886c456f94e412983cbcee97964015e5c9f443d","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A 311 byte Klotski solver in C++ Give it a board, it finds the shortest way to slide the pieces until the big square reaches the goal.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Dream-World-Coder/depuzzled/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint